{
  "id": "Lyo.Video.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Video.Postgres",
  "area": "Plugins",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL and EF Core implementation of `Lyo.Video.IVideoStore`.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL and EF Core implementation of `Lyo.Video.IVideoStore` (`PostgresVideoStore`) via `VideoDbContext`, schema `video`, and `AddPostgresMigrations`. `PostgresVideoStore` implements `Lyo.Health.IHealth`. YouTube link columns live in this schema. The store does not reference `Lyo.Google.Youtube.Client`.",
  "features": [
    "**Schema `video`.** Titles, seasons, episodes, credits, identifiers, YouTube links, genres, alternate titles, collections, and cuts.",
    "**Constraints.** Unique slug, identifier `(scheme, normalized value)` per owner table, season and episode numbers, and one primary cut per movie. `VideoId` is unique across titles and episodes.",
    "**Text.** Stored `tsvector` columns and GIN indexes on movie and episode transcripts.",
    "**DI.** `AddVideoDbContextFactory` / `AddPostgresVideoStore` and `FromConfiguration` overloads (section `PostgresVideo`)."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Registration",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresVideoStore(o => {\n    o.ConnectionString = connStr;\n    o.EnableAutoMigrations = true;\n});"
    }
  ],
